{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Not to us, YHWH, not to us</b> — for our sake, like: \"say to me.\"" "<b>For Your name</b> — which is called upon us. Give glory, and this — that You act for the sake of Your steadfast love."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 115, :notes {0 "The comparison is to לי אמרי (Psalms 116:11), where the ל is likewise 'for'/'on account of'; he parses לא לנו as 'not on our account.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:39.713354647Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}